{"audio": "john-16.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 244800, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1600, "text": "John, Chapter Sixteen."}, {"start_ms": 1600, "end_ms": 5467, "text": "These things have I spoken unto you, that ye should not be offended."}, {"start_ms": 5467, "end_ms": 12933, "text": "They shall put you out of the synagogues: yea, the time cometh, that whosoever killeth you will think that he doeth God service."}, {"start_ms": 12933, "end_ms": 18267, "text": "And these things will they do unto you, because they have not known the Father, nor me."}, {"start_ms": 18267, "end_ms": 23867, "text": "But these things have I told you, that when the time shall come, ye may remember that I told you of them."}, {"start_ms": 23867, "end_ms": 28400, "text": "And these things I said not unto you at the beginning, because I was with you."}, {"start_ms": 28400, "end_ms": 34133, "text": "But now I go my way to him that sent me; and none of you asketh me, Whither goest thou?"}, {"start_ms": 34133, "end_ms": 38267, "text": "But because I have said these things unto you, sorrow hath filled your heart."}, {"start_ms": 38267, "end_ms": 49867, "text": "Nevertheless I tell you the truth; It is expedient for you that I go away: for if I go not away, the Comforter will not come unto you; but if I depart, I will send him unto you."}, {"start_ms": 49867, "end_ms": 65600, "text": "And when he is come, he will reprove the world of sin, and of righteousness, and of judgment: Of sin, because they believe not on me; Of righteousness, because I go to my Father, and ye see me no more; Of judgment, because the prince of this world is judged."}, {"start_ms": 65600, "end_ms": 70533, "text": "I have yet many things to say unto you, but ye cannot bear them now."}, {"start_ms": 70533, "end_ms": 82533, "text": "Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come."}, {"start_ms": 82533, "end_ms": 88000, "text": "He shall glorify me: for he shall receive of mine, and shall shew it unto you."}, {"start_ms": 88000, "end_ms": 95067, "text": "All things that the Father hath are mine: therefore said I, that he shall take of mine, and shall shew it unto you."}, {"start_ms": 95067, "end_ms": 102400, "text": "A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me, because I go to the Father."}, {"start_ms": 102400, "end_ms": 114667, "text": "Then said some of his disciples among themselves, What is this that he saith unto us, A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me: and, Because I go to the Father?"}, {"start_ms": 114667, "end_ms": 118667, "text": "They said therefore, What is this that he saith, A little while?"}, {"start_ms": 118667, "end_ms": 120533, "text": "we cannot tell what he saith."}, {"start_ms": 120533, "end_ms": 133733, "text": "Now Jesus knew that they were desirous to ask him, and said unto them, Do ye inquire among yourselves of that I said, A little while, and ye shall not see me: and again, a little while, and ye shall see me?"}, {"start_ms": 133733, "end_ms": 143600, "text": "Verily, verily, I say unto you, That ye shall weep and lament, but the world shall rejoice: and ye shall be sorrowful, but your sorrow shall be turned into joy."}, {"start_ms": 143600, "end_ms": 155200, "text": "A woman when she is in travail hath sorrow, because her hour is come: but as soon as she is delivered of the child, she remembereth no more the anguish, for joy that a man is born into the world."}, {"start_ms": 155200, "end_ms": 163467, "text": "And ye now therefore have sorrow: but I will see you again, and your heart shall rejoice, and your joy no man taketh from you."}, {"start_ms": 163467, "end_ms": 166133, "text": "And in that day ye shall ask me nothing."}, {"start_ms": 166133, "end_ms": 172800, "text": "Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall ask the Father in my name, he will give it you."}, {"start_ms": 172800, "end_ms": 179467, "text": "Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full."}, {"start_ms": 179467, "end_ms": 187600, "text": "These things have I spoken unto you in proverbs: but the time cometh, when I shall no more speak unto you in proverbs, but I shall shew you plainly of the Father."}, {"start_ms": 187600, "end_ms": 200133, "text": "At that day ye shall ask in my name: and I say not unto you, that I will pray the Father for you: For the Father himself loveth you, because ye have loved me, and have believed that I came out from God."}, {"start_ms": 200133, "end_ms": 206133, "text": "I came forth from the Father, and am come into the world: again, I leave the world, and go to the Father."}, {"start_ms": 206133, "end_ms": 212267, "text": "His disciples said unto him, Lo, now speakest thou plainly, and speakest no proverb."}, {"start_ms": 212267, "end_ms": 220800, "text": "Now are we sure that thou knowest all things, and needest not that any man should ask thee: by this we believe that thou camest forth from God."}, {"start_ms": 220800, "end_ms": 224400, "text": "Jesus answered them, Do ye now believe?"}, {"start_ms": 224400, "end_ms": 235067, "text": "Behold, the hour cometh, yea, is now come, that ye shall be scattered, every man to his own, and shall leave me alone: and yet I am not alone, because the Father is with me."}, {"start_ms": 235067, "end_ms": 239333, "text": "These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace."}, {"start_ms": 239333, "end_ms": 244800, "text": "In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world."}], "words": [{"t": "John,", "s": 162, "e": 446, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 608, "e": 952, "si": 0}, {"t": "Sixteen.", "s": 1033, "e": 1559, "si": 0}, {"t": "These", "s": 2141, "e": 2341, "si": 1}, {"t": "things", "s": 2361, "e": 264